From: Ze kernel maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] rtnetlink: guard original PPP route writers and affected legs

Apply after the original-file link/address guard. The following link-family
dispatch correction is also required before admitting guarded callers.

RTA_OWNER_FD extends the same held original creator-file boundary. Require a
positive PPPIOCGOWNER ABI and the implemented family's ROUTE4/ROUTE6 bit
before submitting any guarded write. There is no fallback without a guard.
Unsupported request shapes and unsupported route families refuse before
their family writer; existing unguarded callers pass NULL authority.

IPv4 checks the constructed next hop and actual replaced/deleted alias under
RTNL before writes or notifications. Unsupported shared/native-nexthop-object
routes refuse even when a first-hop OIF would match. IPv6 takes RTNL around
the guarded operation to retain its original device, then validates actual
old/new candidates under tb6_lock before tree, duplicate-lifetime, flags,
PMTU, sibling, replacement or delete effects. Both gateway-qualified deletion
and delete-all validate every sibling because fib6_del changes their metadata.
No sleeping callback, fget, userspace read or fresh device lookup runs under
tb6_lock. No borrowed authority pointer is stored in a retained route.

RouteReplace semantics remain. Current native PPP's single-device unicast
forms are supported; NH-ID, requested multipath, LWT/encap, cache/source
routes and other unsupported forms refuse. Existing same-owner IPv6 siblings
are supported only after every affected member passes validation.

